# Docs and catalog upkeep

Every manifest change must propagate to **human-facing docs** and **Storybook** — not just code.

## When to update (trigger list)

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| New manifest entry | `docs/08-component-taxonomy.md`, all five runtime README export tables |
| New recipe | `docs/34-public-component-api.md` recipe table |
| Styling/token | `docs/35-styling-and-classnames.md`, WC `tokens.css` header comment |
| Media/VR behavior | `docs/30`, `docs/31`, capability rule cross-link |
| Proof app feature | `docs/43-destination-atlas-proof-apps.md` |
| Builder-only UI | `docs/28-app-component-css-convention.md` — not public npm docs |

## Storybook architecture (do not fork)

Five apps on ports **6006–6010** (WC, React, Vue, Angular, Svelte).

Shared engine: **`tools/storybook-shared/`**

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `palette-catalog/mount-palette-catalog.ts` | Catalog DOM + interactivity |
| `palette-catalog/palette-group-guides.ts` | Group names and docs |
| `palette-catalog/palette-demo-data.ts` | Demo datasets |
| `meta-compositions/` | Dashboard recipe demos + play functions |
| `fixtures.ts`, `storybook-actions.ts` | Shared fixtures |
| `rosettadash-preview.css` | Imports tokens + styles |

Per-runtime story files are **thin wrappers** — import shared mount functions; do not duplicate catalog HTML per framework.

Sidebar taxonomy must match across all five Storybook apps (`docs/38-storybook-component-catalog.md`).

## Story sections (fixed order)

1. **Getting Started/** — `getting-started.stories.*`
2. **Catalog/Components** — palette groups + "All components"
3. **Catalog/Meta components** — live dashboard recipes

## README export tables

Each runtime `packages/*/README.md` maintains a table: subpath, export symbol, CE tag (if any), notes (CE-host, client-only, peers).

Add a row in the **same PR** as the manifest entry.

## Vanilla / HTML docs

Plain HTML consumption is documented on **`packages/web-components/README.md`** — copy-paste snippets with `<script type="module">`, register call, and optional CSS imports. See `vanilla-target.mdc`.

## Numbered docs convention

New topic docs: next free number in `docs/`, linked from `docs/README.md` reading order. When a numbered doc contradicts manifest/code, **fix the doc** or flag in PR — do not silently ignore.

